  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical support to Libya on the monitoring and maintenance of Dams</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 10 September 2023, the northeastern regions of Libya have been severely affected by extensive flooding. Two dams near the eastern town of Derna were destroyed (Abu Mansour and Derna Dams). The storm causes thousands of missing person and inflicted significant damage on critical infrastructure, including healthcare facilities, electricity networks, buildings, roads, and telecommunications. 
Following this disaster, UNESCO and ICOLD joined their efforts and resources to conduct a facts finding mission to acquire a better understanding of the causes of the collapse of both dams, evaluate the damage and provide technical support to Libya in the assessment of the status of Libyan in anticipation of future hydrometeorological risks and set the pathways for dam monitoring and management.</narrative>
  </description>
